/// known-gap: interp `:put` takes no key (the interpreter is being retired)
/// Map keys are text: `:put!(m, 3, x)` writes the key "3", and `m{3}`
/// reads it back, in a small map and in a large one.
m | {}
:put!(m, 3, "x")
:say(m{3})
:say(m{"3"})
:say(:keys(m)[0] == "3")
big | {}
repeat :range(0, 20) as i
    :put!(big, i, i * 2)
xx
:say(big{17})
:say(big{"17"})
:say(m{4})
